{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "singleton blue marker pixels on the background",
  "path": "straight horizontal or vertical sightline toward the unique nearest aligned red 2x2 block, stopping at the adjacent ring cell; markers with no clear sightline do not move",
  "trajectory": "move each selected marker pixel to its stopping cell",
  "dst": "one-cell ring around the matched red 2x2 block",
  "transform": "clear moved marker sources and keep red 2x2 blocks and unmoved marker pixels unchanged",
  "multi_step": "choose nearest clear aligned blocks before moving; a lower-row marker left of a block stays fixed when that block already has selected vertical markers above and below"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10-30 rows x 13-30 cols; background black(0), >=92% background
  colors: block_color=red(2) [observed], marker_color=blue(1) [observed]; exactly 2 foreground colors
  blocks:
    count: 2-4 filled 2x2 blocks of block_color
    separation: min Chebyshev distance >=7 between any two blocks
    edge_margin: block top-left at least 1 cell from grid edge (room for ring)
    some pairs may share row-band or col-band (enables multi-block alignment)
  markers:
    count: 3-15 singleton pixels of marker_color
    moved: 2-12 markers have clear orthogonal sightline to a block and slide to its 1-cell ring
    noise: 1-5 markers with no clear axis-aligned sightline to any block; these stay in place
    distractor: 0-1 lower-left distractor -- marker on bottom row of block, left side, clear path, but block already has vertical markers above AND below; stays fixed
  movement:
    each moved marker travels along a clear (all-bg) horizontal or vertical line to the nearest aligned block
    destination is the orthogonally adjacent ring cell of that block on the same row/col
    travel distance 1-8 cells
    each destination cell is unique (no two markers land on same ring position)
    markers aligned with multiple blocks choose the nearest one by travel distance (unique nearest required)
  output: same grid with moved markers relocated to ring cells; sources cleared to bg; blocks and noise markers unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size (10-30 x 13-30) and pick bg=0, block_color, marker_color (two distinct non-bg colors).
    2. Place 2-4 blocks (2x2) on the grid with pairwise Chebyshev separation >=7 and >=1 cell from all edges.
    3. For each block, choose 1-4 distinct cardinal ring cells as marker destinations (total moved markers 2-12). Ensure unique destination per cell.
    4. For each destination, compute valid source positions: extend the sightline outward from the block by 1-8 cells, ensuring clear bg along the path. Place marker at the source position; this is the input marker location.
    5. Add 1-5 noise markers at random bg cells that are NOT axis-aligned with any block (or have an obstruction on every sightline). Verify no sightline exists.
    6. Optionally add 0-1 lower-left distractor: a marker on bottom-row-left of a block that has both above and below vertical destinations.
    7. Output = input with moved markers shifted to destinations, sources cleared.
